    "https://trinity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Trinity_University/job/Trinity-University-Campus/Operations-Manager---Integrated-Counseling--Health-and-Wellness-Services_JR101649": {
      "title": "Operations Manager - Integrated Counseling, Health and Wellness Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Family Group: Staff Department/Office: Director of Integrated Counseling, Health and Wellness Services Time Type: Full time Compensation: $52,839.34-$66,049.17 Please note, starting salaries are based on factors including internal equity, relevant experience, and education. Exemption Status: Exempt Job Description: The Operations Manager of Integrated Counseling, Health, and Wellness Services (ICHW) provides essential support to the students of Trinity University through supporting the day-to-day operations of the three departments, conducting process assessments, implementing process improvement plans, and facilitating employee development.   Supervision Directs, coordinates and evaluates administrative professionals  Carries out supervisory responsibilities in accordance with all policies and applicable laws Interviews, hires, and trains administrative employees Provides support for all departmental job searches and new employee onboarding    Project Management Develops project implementation plans for various initiatives within the department of ICHW to ensure clear delegation of duties, timeliness of project completion, accurate data tracking, coordination with campus partners and vendors, and appropriate resource allocation Collects and organizes data to better understand the patient/client experience, staff time utilization, resource allocation, and clinical outcomes/metrics Coordinates with the ICHW leadership to create and implement process improvement plans that enhance patient/client experience, resource utilization, and clinical outcomes   Operations Management Manages the collection of fees for service, billing of student accounts, and payment of expenditures within university guidelines Coordinates with campus departments and vendors to resolve issues related to building management, technology support, human resources, and risk management Coordinates the vendor contract-agreement process Oversees expense reporting    ADDITIONAL DUTIES Cooperates and collaborates with other employees in the spirit of teamwork and collegiality and interacts with confidence, patience and integrity to provide professional leadership during emergencies. Complies with all Trinity University policies and guidelines. Performs other duties as required.   EDUCATION  Required:  Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution.   EXPERIENCE Required: Three years of operations related experience.    Preferred: Experience managing the operations of a health center. One year of supervisory experience.   KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Required: Proficiency in the use of English grammar and spelling. Demonstrated skill and proficiency in supervision of staff Accuracy in business math calculations. Advanced administrative and clerical support. Proficiency in Microsoft applications including Word, Excel, PowerPoint. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Must be responsible, dependable and able to maintain confidentiality. Advance knowledge of administrative practices and procedures. Exceptional time management, organizational and problem-solving skills.  Ability to use independent judgment, specialized knowledge and coordination of office functions in a team setting. Must have the ability to multi-task and work cooperatively with others. Experienced with electronic health records.  Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to work and communicate with a diverse population and health care professionals.  Ability to evaluate situations and solve problems; objective and nonjudgmental.  May work under pressure to meet office deadlines and the needs of students.    LICENSES/CERTIFICATIONS Project Management Professional (PMP) Certification    OTHER REQUIREMENTS All jobs require a current Criminal Background Check (CBC). Available for evening or weekend activities.    SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES Supervisor over a section of a department or group of employees.    NUMBER OF DIRECT REPORTS 2   NUMBER OF INDIRECT REPORTS None    SUPERVISION RECEIVED  Limited supervision.  Operates independently.   INTERACTION  Works alone Works with other employees Students Vendors"
    },
    "https://trinity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Trinity_University/job/Trinity-University-Campus/Residential-Life-Coordinator_JR101648": {
      "title": "Residential Life Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Family Group: Staff Department/Office: Assistant Director Residential Life Time Type: Full time Compensation: $39,484.62-$49,355.78 Please note, starting salaries are based on factors including internal equity, relevant experience, and education. Exemption Status: Exempt Job Description: Responsible for the supervision of paraprofessional student staff members. Responsible for facilitating student development through educational programming and the overall management of all aspects of health and safety within multiple residence halls.   Supervises, trains, evaluates and selects Resident Assistant staff. Facilitates the development of a community and educational environment which encourages inclusive and positive relationships among students through social and educational programming.  Provides support and resources to students in individual meetings. Counsels, advises and assists residents concerning personal, interpersonal and facilities concerns. Uses multiple software platforms, including THD, StarRez, Maxient, etc., to track and direct operational components of the residence hall move-in/move-out, student conduct and student wellness processes. Coordinates and implements all aspects of an assigned program area, including first-year, sophomore year and upper-division experience. Acts as a liaison between residents and Facilities Services, ensuring all maintenance and housekeeping requests are completed in a timely manner. Serves as the primary point of contact for the students in their residence halls with a variety of presenting issues, including mental health issues, academic struggles, interpersonal conflicts, etc.  Assists students which requires collaboration with parents and professional staff and faculty in Student Affairs and Academic Affairs. Manages Resident Assistant program budget, through receipt reconciliation and Purchase Card oversight. Enforces and supports Trinity University and Residential Life policies, processes and protocols. Serves on a variety of Student Life committees including CAS Review committees and search committees.  Serves as a Campus Security Authority (CSA), as defined by the Clery Act of 1998.  Serves as Summer Housing Coordinator, as assigned. Reports all relevant details about alleged sexual misconduct involving any student, faculty or staff about which they know or have reason to know. ADDITIONAL DUTIES Serves in the after hours on-call duty rotation for approximately 10 to 13 weeks throughout the calendar year. Cooperates and collaborates with other employees in the spirit of teamwork and collegiality and interacts with confidence, patience and integrity to provide professional leadership during emergencies. Complies with all Trinity University policies and guidelines. Performs other duties as required. EDUCATION Required: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. Preferred: Master's degree or equivalent from an accredited institution. EXPERIENCE Required: One year of experience working in a Residential Life office as an undergraduate, graduate, or professional staff member on a college campus. Preferred: One to two years of professional live-in experience. Demonstrate experience and initiative with student and community development. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Required: Possess a commitment and ability to create communities that are inclusive of diverse populations. Excellent interpersonal, communication and leadership skills. Proven ability to manage crises, resolve conflicts and make sound decisions under pressure. Ability to manage confidential and sensitive information. Effective time management skills."
    },
    "https://trinity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Trinity_University/job/Trinity-University-Campus/Vivarium-Technician_JR101641-1": {
      "title": "Vivarium Technician",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Family Group: Staff Department/Office: D. R. Semmes School of Science Time Type: Full time Compensation: $18.98-$23.73 Please note, starting salaries are based on factors including internal equity, relevant experience, and education. Exemption Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: The Vivarium Technician maintains the animal care facility and provides consistent, high-quality husbandry services in accordance with Trinity University policies and procedures. The position operates and maintains facility equipment and supports the daily care of research animals housed at the institution. The Vivarium Technician is expected to be self-motivated, dependable, attentive to detail, and able to work independently with minimal supervision.   JOB DUTIES Provides daily husbandry for multiple laboratory animal species, including health checks and observations; feeding; monitoring automatic and manual watering systems; changing and cleaning animal cages, racks, and related accessories; and safely handling and restraining animals. Provides animal-room services, including maintaining complete and accurate daily room logs; monitoring expiration dates for consumables; following special husbandry instructions associated with approved research needs; and sanitizing rooms, surfaces, and equipment using appropriate disinfectants and detergents. Operates cage-wash and sanitation equipment. Prepares cages, racks, transport carts, and related equipment for washing by breaking down caging, removing bedding and waste, and dumping or scraping cages as required. Reassembles and prepares clean caging and equipment for use. Stocks and maintains husbandry and facility supplies, including personal protective equipment, animal feed, bedding, enrichment materials, cleaning products, and other consumables. Reports low inventory, equipment malfunctions, and facility concerns promptly. Complies with institutional health and safety requirements, general laboratory practices, approved IACUC protocols and policies, standard operating procedures, and applicable animal-welfare requirements. Participates in required training and promptly reports animal-health, safety, or compliance concerns. ADDITIONAL DUTIES Cooperates and collaborates with other employees in the spirit of teamwork and collegiality and interacts with confidence, patience, and integrity. Complies with all Trinity University policies and guidelines. Performs other duties as assigned. EDUCATION Required: High school diploma or equivalent. Preferred: Bachelor’s degree in biology or animal sciences. EXPERIENCE Required: One year of experience in animal care, laboratory animal husbandry, veterinary care, research support, or a related setting. Preferred: Three years of experience in animal care, laboratory animal husbandry, veterinary care, research support, or a related setting. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Required: Ability to learn and consistently follow animal care, safety, sanitation, and facility procedures. Ability to recognize and promptly report changes in animal health, behavior, food or water consumption, and environmental conditions. Ability to safely handle and restrain multiple laboratory animal species after appropriate training. Time and task management skills, including the ability to complete scheduled care activities reliably and accurately. Organization, recordkeeping, and written and verbal communication skills. Preferred: Knowledge of laboratory animal care practices, biosecurity principles, and IACUC requirements. LICENSES/CERTIFICATIONS Preferred: AALAS Assistant Laboratory Animal Technician (ALAT) certification, or willingness to pursue certification. OTHER REQUIREMENTS All jobs require a current Criminal Background Check (CBC). Ability to work scheduled weekends, holidays, and emergency or overtime assignments as required to maintain continuous animal care. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES None. DECISION MAKING Performs recurring work under established procedures while exercising judgment to identify and promptly report unusual animal-health, facility, equipment, safety, or research conditions. BUDGET RESPONSIBILITY None. FINANCIAL RESPONSIBILITY None."
    },
    "https://trinity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Trinity_University/job/Trinity-University-Campus/Peace-Officer_JR101622-1": {
      "title": "Police Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Family Group: Staff Department/Office: Sergeant of Patrol Time Type: Full time Compensation: $23.97-$29.96 Please note, starting salaries are based on factors including internal equity, relevant experience, and education. Exemption Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Trinity University Police Department Full-Time | Trinity University Campus | Starting Pay: $28.85/hour The Trinity University Police Department is seeking a TCOLE-certified Police Officer to serve and protect the Trinity University community. As a Trinity University Police Officer, you will help provide a safe and welcoming campus environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Officers are expected to exercise sound judgment, professionalism, integrity, and respect while enforcing applicable laws and University policies. This role requires an officer who understands that effective campus policing is about more than enforcement. It requires building relationships, providing service, communicating effectively, responding appropriately during emergencies, and treating every member of the community with dignity and respect.   Starting Pay: $28.85 per hour IMPORTANT: Applicants must currently hold a Texas Commission on Law Enforcement (TCOLE) Peace Officer license or must be TCOLE certified before their first day of employment. What You’ll Do As a Police Officer with Trinity University, you will: Patrol the Trinity University campus by vehicle, bicycle, and on foot. Respond to calls for service and provide assistance to students, employees, and visitors. Conduct preliminary and follow-up investigations involving criminal and non-criminal incidents occurring on University property. Preserve the peace and protect life and property using lawful, professional, and appropriate policing practices. Enforce applicable federal, state, and local laws, including traffic laws and regulations. Conduct traffic stops and issue warnings or citations when appropriate. Make arrests and take individuals into custody when circumstances and applicable law require. Help ensure University buildings, facilities, and property remain safe and secure. Prepare clear, accurate, and timely police reports and other required documentation. Provide information, assistance, and directions to members of the University community and campus visitors. Respond quickly and exercise sound judgment during emergency and high-pressure situations. Work collaboratively with fellow officers, University departments, and external law enforcement and emergency response partners. Follow Trinity University policies, departmental procedures, and applicable laws and regulations. Perform other related duties as assigned. What We’re Looking For Successful Trinity University Police Officers demonstrate: Professionalism, integrity, and sound judgment. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. The ability to remain composed and make rational decisions during emergencies and stressful situations. A commitment to treating individuals with dignity and respect. Strong observation, documentation, and report-writing skills. The ability to interpret and appropriately apply laws, policies, procedures, and departmental directives. A service-oriented approach to working within a diverse university community. The ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team. Required Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Current TCOLE Peace Officer license/certification or must be TCOLE certified before their first day of employment. Valid Texas driver’s license and an acceptable driving record. Ability to meet all applicable requirements for employment as a Texas peace officer. Ability to successfully complete Trinity University’s required pre-employment screening and background investigation. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Criminal Justice or a related field. Two or more years of experience in law enforcement, security, criminal justice, or a related field. Previous experience working in a campus, community-oriented, or service-focused policing environment. Schedule This is a full-time, 40-hour-per-week position. Police Officers must be available to work rotating shifts, weekends, holidays, overtime, and emergency assignments as required. Because the Trinity University Police Department provides continuous campus coverage, schedules may vary based on departmental and University needs. Physical and Working Requirements Police Officers must be able to perform the essential physical responsibilities associated with law enforcement duties, including: Walking and running Standing and sitting for extended periods Climbing stairs Jumping Lifting or moving objects weighing 50 pounds or more Riding a bicycle Operating a motor vehicle Working outdoors and in inclement weather Responding to emergency and potentially hazardous situations Officers may be required to use or operate law enforcement and communications equipment associated with their duties, including authorized firearms, intermediate weapons, radios, vehicles, and other departmental equipment. Pre-Employment Requirements Employment is contingent upon successfully completing all required pre-employment processes, which may include: Comprehensive background investigation Physical examination Drug screening Psychological evaluation Driving-record review Verification of TCOLE licensing and eligibility Other screenings or requirements applicable to employment as a Texas peace officer Applicants must meet applicable legal and licensing standards regarding criminal history and eligibility to serve as a peace officer. Supervision Work is performed under the direction of departmental supervisory personnel and is reviewed through observation, reports, performance standards, and other established departmental practices. Attendance Regular and reliable attendance is an essential function of this position. Officers are expected to work their assigned schedules and any required scheduled or emergency overtime. Serve. Protect. Be Part of the Community. At Trinity University, policing is both a public safety responsibility and a community partnership. Our officers have the opportunity to know the community they serve, build relationships across campus, and contribute directly to an environment where students, employees, and visitors can learn, work, and thrive safely. If you are a TCOLE-certified peace officer or in the process of completing your TCOLE certification who values professionalism, service, accountability, and community engagement, we encourage you to apply. Starting Pay: $28.85 per hour | Full-Time | Required TCOLE certified before their first day of employment."
    },
    "https://trinity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Trinity_University/job/Trinity-University-Campus/Assistant-Professor-of-Classical-Studies---Greek_JR101647": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Classical Studies - Greek",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Family Group: Faculty Time Type: Full time Department/Office: Classical Studies Exemption Status: Exempt Job Description: The Department of Classical Studies at Trinity University invites applications for a tenure-track position in Classical Studies, beginning in August 2027, at the rank of Assistant Professor. The department is seeking a dynamic and innovative teacher with an active research profile who has a demonstrated ability in and enthusiasm for teaching ancient Greek language and literature at all levels and Latin up to the intermediate level and who specializes in the ancient Greek world, broadly defined. Particular areas of research and teaching that are attractive to us include Greek history, culture, and literature; multicultural approaches to the ancient Mediterranean world; ancient and modern reception of Classical texts and culture; or digital humanities. Candidates must demonstrate a strong research profile and a firm commitment to teaching at the undergraduate level. The successful candidate will be expected to teach introductory courses while developing upper-division courses in their area of specialization. The ideal candidate will have a facility for interdisciplinary teaching and interest in mentoring students in undergraduate research projects, including in the summer. All faculty are expected to contribute to Pathways, the University’s interdisciplinary general education program.   BACKGROUND Trinity University is a secular, independent, private institution, founded in 1869. Trinity offers high-quality science, liberal arts, and pre-professional programs as represented by the four schools (STEM, Arts & Humanities, Social Science and Civic Engagement, and Business) to approximately 2,500 undergraduate students from the U.S. and more than 45 countries. The attractive campus overlooks downtown San Antonio, a city rich in heritage and ethnic diversity. Additional information can be found on the Resource Guide to Trinity & San Antonio . The Carlos Alvarez School of Arts and Humanities, endowed with a gift of $25 million , is at the center of Trinity's liberal arts education. Faculty are international leaders in their respective fields, creating engaged learning experiences grounded in careful study of tradition, critical thinking, clear communication, and creative expression. Classical Studies at Trinity is a vibrant department with six tenured / tenure-track faculty and strong connections with other departments on campus, including Anthropology, Art History, Philosophy, and Religion. We encourage our students to pursue undergraduate research, often in collaboration with faculty, and we have been active participants in our university’s summer undergraduate research program. The department participates in a faculty-led study abroad summer course in Rome and in a faculty-led archaeological dig in Cyprus . Both the Department of Classical Studies  and the University as a whole value and safeguard academic freedom for faculty members in their teaching and scholarship. Trinity is guided by a set of core values and is committed to implementing practices in pursuit of an inclusive campus for all students, faculty, and staff to feel welcomed and engaged in a community of learning.   DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Teaching   Teach Classical Greek at all levels and Latin to the intermediate level. Teach both lower and upper-level courses in the candidate’s area of interest and expertise. Offer courses that complement departmental offerings and contribute to the Pathways general education curriculum, including the First Year Experience, under a (typically) 3-2 teaching load. Advise departmental majors and minors.    Research Maintain a consistent and productive program of scholarship, to include publication of research, presentations of papers at academic conferences, attendance at professional meetings, and participation in professional organizations.    Service Provide appropriate service to the department, the university, and the profession. QUALIFICATIONS EDUCATION Required: Ph.D. or A.B.D. in Classics or related field. A.B.D. candidates must present evidence that Ph.D. will have been completed and accepted no later than August 2027. Preferred: Teaching experience, as Instructor of Record or Teaching Assistant (or equivalent) in an undergraduate course related to ancient Greek, Latin, or Classics. EXPERIENCE Preferred: The ideal candidate will have a facility for interdisciplinary teaching and interest in mentoring students in undergraduate research projects, including in the summer. ATTENDANCE All teaching for this position will be conducted in person.  HOW TO APPLY For internal applicants , please apply through Workday using the ' Jobs Hub ' application, see instructions provided here . For external applicants , when starting the application, select \"Apply Manually.” Only complete fields with a red asterisk, which are required. Please create your Workday application account using a personal email address , as you will need to maintain access to this account throughout the pre-hire process, if selected.  For all applicants , you do not need to complete the “(Work) Experience,” “Education,” “Certifications,” or “Languages” fields - these details will be provided in your curriculum vitae. In the “Application Documents” field, please upload the following as seen below.  File 1: A cover letter File 2: A curriculum vitae File 3:  A teaching portfolio, including (i) a statement of teaching philosophy that addresses your teaching interests and abilities; (ii) sample syllabi; and (iii) teaching evaluations (if available) File 4: A writing sample File 5: Intentional inclusion statement - Intentional Inclusion is a core value at Trinity University. Please provide a brief (1-2 page) reflection on the ways that you might contribute to cultivating an environment where people feel welcomed, respected, and empowered to reach their full potential. Provide examples of how that relates to your teaching, research/scholarship and other professional activities. In addition, please arrange that three letters of recommendation be sent to classics@trinity.edu .  Review of applications will begin on November   3,   2026. CONTACT INFORMATION Nicolle Hirschfeld nhirschf@trinity.edu Please ensure that all required documents are uploaded prior to submitting an application. If you have revisions needed to an application already submitted or need help submitting an application, please contact Human Resources at 210-999-7507 or email humanresources@trinity.edu ."
    },
    "https://trinity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Trinity_University/job/Trinity-University-Campus/Athletic-Trainer---Sports-Camp_JR101645": {
      "title": "Athletic Trainer - Sports Camp",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Family Group: Staff Department/Office: Recreation and Sports Camps Time Type: Part time Compensation: Please note, starting salaries are based on factors including internal equity, relevant experience, and education. Exemption Status: Exempt Job Description: Responsible for the coordination and administration of all aspects of the athletic training room and sports medicine offerings for the intercollegiate athletic programs as deemed by the Head Athletic Trainer.   Onsite care and management of injuries and illnesses including: prevention, evaluation, management and rehabilitation. Provides accommodation recommendations, related to sport, for student athletes with restrictions or limitations. Assists with accident insurance claims processing.  Minimizes risk of injury through awareness, education and prevention strategies.  Maintains student athlete insurance information. Assists with training, scheduling and payroll for student staff. Assists with physical examinations and screenings. Assists with drug testing per department policy.  Makes appropriate physician’s referrals and appointments. Communicates with physicians and coaching staff regarding the injury status of athletes. Assists the Athletic Director and coaching staff in determining whether the athletic facility is in optimal and safe condition.  Helps monitor weather conditions and dangerous environments (humidity/lightning). Coordinates the purchasing and use of all equipment and supplies needed for the operation of the athletic training facility, in accordance with University policies. Adheres to conference guidelines, including visiting team accommodations and services. ADDITIONAL DUTIES  Abides by NCAA Division III rules and regulations. Cooperates and collaborates with other employees in the spirit of teamwork and collegiality and interacts with confidence, patience and integrity to provide professional leadership during emergencies. Complies with all Trinity University policies and guidelines. Performs other duties as required. EDUCATION  Required: Bachelor's degree from four-year college or university. Preferred: Master's degree or equivalent from four-year college or university. EXPERIENCE  Required: 1 year of experience with an intercollegiate athletic program. Administrative experience with operating an athletic training room. Preferred: 3 years of experience. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES  Required: Knowledge of a large range of medical problems.  Assessment, evaluation skills and working with other healthcare professionals. Ability to think critically and make independent decisions regarding the assessment, treatment, rehabilitation and return to play decisions per state licensure guidelines. Thorough and detailed with injury tracking and documentation. Ability to communicate effectively in high stress/pressure situations when talking to patients, medical professionals, staff and families. Preferred: Ability to organize, prioritize and perform multiple tasks with little or no supervision. Therapeutic rehabilitation. Injury evaluation. Therapeutic modality usage. Manual therapy techniques. Documentation. LICENSES/CERTIFICATIONS  Required: Must possess a valid Texas Driver’s License and have a good driving history.  May not have more than two moving violations in a three-year period. NATA BOC certification CPR/AED/First Aid OTHER REQUIREMENTS All jobs require a current Criminal Background Check (CBC). Requires the hours of work necessary to fulfill responsibilities which may include evenings, weekends and traveling with teams."
    },
    "https://trinity.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Trinity_University/job/Trinity-University-Campus/Part-Time-Assistant-Athletic-Trainer_JR101644": {
      "title": "Part Time Assistant Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Family Group: Staff Department/Office: Athletic Trainers Time Type: Part time Compensation: Please note, starting salaries are based on factors including internal equity, relevant experience, and education. Exemption Status: Non-Exempt Job Description: Responsible for the coordination and administration of all aspects of the athletic training room and sports medicine offerings for the intercollegiate athletic programs as deemed by the Head Athletic Trainer.   JOB DUTIES Onsite care and management of injuries and illnesses including: prevention, evaluation, management and rehabilitation. Provides accommodation recommendations, related to sport, for student athletes with restrictions or limitations. Assists with accident insurance claims processing.  Minimizes risk of injury through awareness, education and prevention strategies.  Maintains student athlete insurance information. Assists with training, scheduling and payroll for student staff. Assists with physical examinations and screenings. Assists with drug testing per department policy.  Makes appropriate physician’s referrals and appointments. Communicates with physicians and coaching staff regarding the injury status of athletes. Assists the Athletic Director and coaching staff in determining whether the athletic facility is in optimal and safe condition.  Helps monitor weather conditions and dangerous environments (humidity/lightning). Coordinates the purchasing and use of all equipment and supplies needed for the operation of the athletic training facility, in accordance with University policies. Adheres to conference guidelines, including visiting team accommodations and services. ADDITIONAL DUTIES  Abides by NCAA Division III rules and regulations. Cooperates and collaborates with other employees in the spirit of teamwork and collegiality and interacts with confidence, patience and integrity to provide professional leadership during emergencies. Complies with all Trinity University policies and guidelines. Performs other duties as required.   EDUCATION  Required: Bachelor's degree from four-year college or university.   Preferred: Master's degree or equivalent from four-year college or university.   EXPERIENCE  Required: One year of experience with an intercollegiate athletic program. Administrative experience with operating an athletic training room.   Preferred: Three years of experience."
    },
